          "worked": "Let $u=2x^3$ and $v=5-4x$. Then $u'=6x^2$ and $v'=-4$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y'&=\\frac{6x^2(5-4x)-2x^3(-4)}{(5-4x)^2}\\\\y'&=\\frac{2x^2(15-8x)}{(5-4x)^2}\\end{align*}$$",
